WEBVTT

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.150
Welcome.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.150
Oh my, aren't you a cute waitress.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.650
I wonder if you're about the same age as my child.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.000
So, you're here at last?

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.760
Senpai, why is this happening?

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.560
What?

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.060
You're closing the café and going to America.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.770
I heard it from the newspaper club.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.320
There's a rumour amongst the
students with part-time jobs at the café.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.690
No, that's...

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.780
So, it's about that?

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.740
Senpai, you said that place was filled with memories of your mother,

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.040
and you went through all that trouble to buy it back, so why?

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.170
That's...

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.670
...because I promised my father.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:38.920
I think my father wanted me to choose to study of my own free will.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.300
To return to America, I have to stop running the café.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.970
Didn't you say the café was doing well?

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:46.890
Yes.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.690
It's managing somehow right now, but eventually it will go bankrupt.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.230
It seems even though I'm capable with maths,

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.280
business is not my strong point.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.700
No, that's more a problem of sense than business.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.040
Senpai, I think I understand, so I'll help you.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.670
I'll help at the café, so let's think of a way to bring lots of customers!

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.510
Mikadono Shougo-kun.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.840
He's a far more amusing guy than I had imagined.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.060
What am I supposed to think when he
suddenly proposes to reorganise my café?

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.680
Even if he has the blood of Mikadono Kumagorou,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.490
he's still just a novice.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:40.320
There's no way he can save a café from going bankrupt.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.740
But it's okay like this.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.990
Sooner or later, it will end up according to plan.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.380
What are you writing?

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.750
A draft for an advert.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.460
A draft for an advert?

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.340
What's that?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.070
All right! It's done!

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.880
Ah, wait! Where are you going?

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.800
The manga club.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.640
The manga club's room.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.560
Draw a moe picture for this advert?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.480
Because I heard that you're the best in the school at it, Tanaka-kun.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.690
Well, not the best...

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.320
I'm relying on you, so I'll give you my gratitude.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:24.450
What?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.740
You'll do an interview for The Miryuuin Times?

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.670
Oh, the president laughed with five "ku"s.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.000
That means she's in a good mood.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.630
So it has come to this after all.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.710
Mikadono Shougo,

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.640
even if you have the blood of an emperor,

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:49.140
the interweaved webs of fate in the
spinning wheel of time will pull you back!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.310
Um... I don't really understand what you're saying,

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.230
but before I do the interview, I have one condition.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:00.940
I want you to run this Lyrical Sisters advert in The Miryuuin Times.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.490
Hmm... very well.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.950
That concludes the business, then.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.540
What have you been sighing about?

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.630
This time I'm making leaflets,

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:16.790
but I was wondering if there's anything else I could do.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.330
To do something like that here,

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.250
you're really putting a lot of effort into it, aren't you?

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.840
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.390
Um... why do I have to wear this?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:34.020
You were going to help me throughout the event, weren't you?

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.060
Then you have to properly become a sister.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:37.980
But...

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.270
The outfit is only like that for the time being,

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.690
but since Tsuruma-san is an honours student who studies too much,

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.440
I wonder if you can handle being a waitress.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.240
Ah, hey!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.120
I can do it properly!

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.700
Eh, really?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.200
It's all right!

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.960
I'll show you that I can properly become a moe-moe waitress!

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.180
D-Did you see them?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.550
I wasn't looking. I saw them, but I wasn't looking.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.930
What's up with this tail?

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.020
It has a special mechanism in it.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:20.770
It's equipped to respond to your emotions.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.570
What kind of mechanism is that?

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.820
It's patent-pending, so it's a company secret!

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.660
Well, now that I've seen Tsuruma's bad girl panties...

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.780
I don't have bad girl panties!

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.290
I'm going to my club activities now.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.790
Ah, Miyabi!

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.540
Do your best in swimming practice!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.300
I'm looking forward to see you in the tournament.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:46.710
Yeah!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:55.680
If you put the half-cooked omelette on top of the chicken rice...

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.040
...and do this...

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.440
...you can make the omelette like this.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.770
That's great!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:04.360
You're good at cooking, just like I heard, Kunitachi-san.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.800
It's nothing special enough to say it's great.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.150
Where did you learn this?

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:12.160
It's only from studying the necessities of marriage and practising at home.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.410
What's vital is the taste.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.180
Don't worry!

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.800
It's delicious!

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:19.790
President Tendou!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.000
Since when have you been here?

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.210
Don't worry about it.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.000
All right!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:31.180
I'll put that on the menu immediately with the name "Domineering little sister's high-class lady omelette".

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:33.890
Huh, domineering?

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:36.850
I'm not really domineering...

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.390
Don't worry about it.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.190
Being domineering has its own moe factor.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.850
No, that's not what I mean...

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.650
That's not right, is it?

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.480
I'm not domineering, right?

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.910
I'm going.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:55.780
All right, come on!

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:09.090
That's good, Konoe.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.900
Just like that.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:11.760
Y-Yes.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:19.970
Keep your composure about you and control the tail's movements.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.230
I understand.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.810
I understand, but...

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.380
When I think about wearing this in front of people,

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.360
I get embarrassed and my heart beats harder.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:32.990
Are you all right?

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.200
Ah, yes. Eh?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:42.870
Oh! Tsuruma is wearing panties with a surprisingly interesting design.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.170
This is an unexpected moe point.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.580
I wonder if I should make a sketch.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.840
Shougo-san! The tail!

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.130
Do something about the tail!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.710
U-Understood.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:55.050
N-Not there!

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:56.970
T-Then, what about here?

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.430
T-There, too...

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.470
Then what about here?

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.470
Or maybe here?

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.150
Here?

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:08.400
Or is it here?

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.570
Nyaaa~

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:17.450
The event week starts this Saturday!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.200
It comes with a service ticket, so if you like, you can-

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.500
Ah, it's Onii-chan-senpai!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:23.950
Huh?

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:27.880
Onii-chan-senpai, please give me one too!

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.460
Ah, here you go.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.210
By the way, what's with calling me "Onii-chan-senpai"?

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:38.590
It's common amongst the first year girls to call Mikadono-senpai "Onii-chan-senpai".

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:42.310
You're our senior, but you have an "ideal Onii-chan" aura.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.270
Really?

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.270
Well then, Onii-chan-senpai.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.150
Give it your best!

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.730
Onii-chan-senpai.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.690
Thank you for your efforts so early in the morning.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.700
I came early with my bag, so I'll help you out.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.790
Ah, you're from Lyrical Sisters.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.660
I'm a first year, Kashinoki Kurumi.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.330
So you're a student here?

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.080
Yes!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:14.090
Let's do our best together to liven up the café!

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:17.090
Yeah, of course.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:37.950
Onii-chan, thanks for waiting!

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:38.930
Eh?

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.700
But I didn't order this.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.080
This is on the house from the café, nyan~

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.330
Welcome home, Onee-chan!

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.340
We're back, little sister!

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.130
It's pretty lively in here, isn't it?

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:00.050
Yep, it's been pretty busy since this morning.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:03.100
Oh! Kunitachi, President Tendou!

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.510
You came at a good time!

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.150
Welcome home, Onee-chan!

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.230
W-Welcome home, Onee-chan...

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.160
Hey, it's mean of you to laugh...

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.160
N-No...

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.790
Miyabi, you came!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.870
I'm late because on Sunday we have practice until lunch.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.460
Thanks for coming.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.930
It's Onii-chan-senpai!

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.130
It really is!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.380
Hey!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.510
Can we have a picture taken with you, please?

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:40.070
Eh?

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:40.760
With me?

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:41.470
Yes!

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.840
I'm next!

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.260
I'm after her!

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.970
Hey, we saw him first!

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.140
That's right, that's right!

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.850
Hey Shougo-kun.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.020
I heard you were busy, so I came to help you out.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:11.210
O-Onee-chan, would you like some more tea?

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.010
T-Thank you.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.210
I'd like to have some more.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.140
How is it, Senpai?

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.410
Even after this event week has finished,

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.480
the number of customers hasn't dropped.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:36.100
If we increase the number of regulars, then our sales will grow.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:36.770
Then...

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.530
By the look of things, it seems like the café can continue to stay open.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.490
We've done it, Senpai!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.440
Yep, we did it.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.240
Thank goodness!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.250
I'm really glad!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.670
Hey, Mikadono.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.250
What is it, Senpai?

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.000
Will you marry me?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.800
Heh?!

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.880
What are you asking me, all of a sudden?!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.920
You gave my café a makeover.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:09.850
It's just what you'd expect from the man who inherited Mikadono Kumagorou's blood.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.890
Share those powerful genes with me!

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:15.140
Genes?!

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:19.650
After the reassortment of our chromosomes,

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.400
our management ability and sense of moe will be combined,

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.240
and we'd have the strongest child.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.660
Let's not waste time and start right now.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.930
Please stop joking.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.000
I'm being serious.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:47.630
Hello?

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.220
Hey, Shougo-kun.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.670
Oh, it's you, Ikusu.

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:53.890
It looks like I forgot my hat and left it in the café.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:56.140
I'm sorry, but can you look for it?

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.280
Shougo-kun.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.780
Ikusu... Why?

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.820
I had a look, but there is no hat inside.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:13.990
You...

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.330
Did I... interrupt something?

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.960
You weren't spying, were you?

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.250
Who knows...

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:25.710
Anyway, after I did some research on the mobile phone,

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.130
I found a name which worries me.

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:29.930
Sagara Mei.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:35.140
The author of the technology paper about the voice changer feature turns out to be her.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.730
So that means...

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.020
Senpai talked about it.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.400
The paper that she made her money from...

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.410
It didn't ring.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:54.910
It looks like I wake up at this time out of habit now.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.300
Don't tell me... That's...

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.090
I see!

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:12.050
If she's over there, she can see my room clearly.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:16.560
And so, she uses that phone and calls me every morning.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:20.560
But why did she go out of her way to do that?

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.620
Oh! You're here so early in the morning.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.880
It's still too early for an afternoon nap.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.700
The little sister from the phone was here all along,

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.220
looking into my room, right?

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:54.940
Goodness...

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:57.180
It seems like you've finally realised.

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:01.180
You've been calling me every morning, haven't you, Senpai?

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:06.050
You developed it based on your own paper, and you used the mobile phone.

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:09.940
Since you've already figured that much out,
there's no point in pretending to be innocent.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.410
Now we can start everything anew.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.080
But I made one mistake.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:24.040
After you suggested that we should
work together to reorganise the café,

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:27.130
I thought without a doubt that you were becoming interested in me.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:29.460
But I was so quickly rejected.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:34.260
Senpai, do you remember what happened on the day of Father's funeral service?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:37.100
Yes, I remember it well.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:41.770
In any case, I spoke to you for the first time on that day.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.600
I haven't forgotten about it either.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.150
The weather was great on that day, wasn't it?

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.750
That's right.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:51.280
The sky was so blue it was sad.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.780
Senpai, I'm doubting you right now.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.400
Really?

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:01.260
So that was a trap, after all?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:05.240
I didn't think that forgetfulness would be used as proof.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:07.590
I thought I'd managed to fool you.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:09.540
But it seems you weren't that naive.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.170
That's right.

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:13.170
It was snowing on that day.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:17.760
When did you realise that I wasn't actually your little sister?

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.350
I'm only sure of it just now.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.020
But at first, I thought it was strange,

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:28.860
because why would my "little sister" call me every morning at the same time?

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.280
And so, after thinking back upon it for a while,

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:35.820
just about everything seemed to be too good to be true.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:39.530
It's as if everything was planned right from the beginning.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.870
I see.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:45.120
That was well thought out.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:50.000
First of all, attacking you with a morning phone call meant that you wouldn't get enough sleep.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:53.260
She would wait for you to approach the infirmary,

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.970
and lead you to her hiding place.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:18:01.850
There, she would let you see that she has the same mobile phone as Tsuruma-kun.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.430
At first I intended to use the naughty magazine as bait.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:08.480
It was my intention to let you find it by yourself.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.610
It went surprisingly well.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:17.570
Senpai's plan was to use the café failing as a pretext to go to America,

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:21.870
while I thought she was my little sister.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:26.520
Mikadono, you really surprised me.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:30.130
I didn't think you'd really be able to save my café.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:34.920
With her pretext for returning to America gone,

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.520
she got closer to you that night.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:42.260
Of course, she probably foresaw that you wouldn't accept her.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:45.640
I thought it was a good idea,

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:49.810
but I was defeated as my goal drew near.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:53.060
I couldn't stand being here a moment longer, so I tried to escape to America.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:59.360
She was in the process of preparing to escape, and was waiting for you to realise that she was the little sister this time.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:02.660
Then, when I questioned her...

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:06.410
She was hoping to take her assets and go to America.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:09.600
In order to keep the identity of the little sister safe,

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:11.750
she would disappear to the other side of the ocean.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.130
So that was the outline of the plot, huh?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.600
My, my...

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:24.300
I meant to tell you myself, but it looks like my plan failed.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:31.270
Senpai, why did you try to deceive me this way?

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.940
I couldn't figure it out, right to the end.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.940
But now I finally understand.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:45.030
Senpai, you were trying to avert my eyes from my real little sister in order not to fall behind, am I wrong?

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:56.040
I met her at my mother's café when I was still a child.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:20:00.150
We got on really well right away.

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:04.340
My mum said it seemed like we were actual siblings.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.650
Senpai, I beg of you.

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:09.100
Please tell me who my little sister is!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.820
I won't.

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:11.600
Why?

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.980
She's an illegitimate child.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.000
She is something the Mikadono family does not wish for.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.680
In any case,

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:24.240
would you be able to welcome her warmly into your family?

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.990
Or rather, would you treat her like a burden?

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:31.620
I don't want her to go through that.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:35.580
If it's like that, it would be better if she weren't there in the first place.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.130
If that's the case....

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.050
If that's the case, I'll protect her.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.010
Even if other people are in denial,

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:46.180
I'll accept her as my little sister... as a member of my family!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:57.480
I understand.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.440
Then...

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.820
But I still can't tell you right now.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:05.570
If you can actually protect your sister,

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.870
and I am confident that it is within your power to do so,

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:11.120
I'll tell you about her.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:18.290
Honestly, you're a soft touch for dropping it after that.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.800
Maybe I am...

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:42.780
Mikadono Shougo...

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.990
You really are a strange person.

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:48.870
Senpai, can I ask you for one last favour?

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.030
Favour?

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:55.910
Please continue to get on well with my little sister.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:04.050
But he seems like a pretty good big brother.

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:25.150
The love that ran away is searching for Eden

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:36.750
Despite losing my bearings, I understood the weight I felt from you

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:42.380
We felt it on that summer day

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:48.470
Do you regret our meeting because of these painful lies?

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:54.470
Are you saying it was only painful?

00:22:54.470 --> 00:23:02.110
Sweep away the coming tomorrow with those gentle hands

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:08.190
A promise forever from bygone days

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:14.950
We will certainly be together, because I still believe in you

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:20.960
My pounding heart won't stop now

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:27.050
It has finally begun, that lovely thing

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:38.770
To a dazzling world of bewilderment with my heavenly lover

00:23:40.810 --> 00:23:42.270
Shougo-san!

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:45.150
Caress my cream puffs, nya~n!

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:48.290
No, do something good with me instead, nya~n!

00:23:48.290 --> 00:23:50.190
Um, hey, we have the preview to do, so...

00:23:50.190 --> 00:23:53.120
Forget about that and hurry over here, nya~n!

00:23:53.120 --> 00:23:55.910
If you don't, you'll get licked by me, nya~n!

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:58.670
I'm okay with being licked, nya~n!

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:02.160
Next time, episode 7: Little Sister's Rules are Honest and Beautiful!

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:04.860
How on earth did it get like this?!

00:24:05.640 --> 00:24:08.900
The secret power of the king of the black cats has been realised!
